Regenerated against 9d2a6c1. The first attempt conflicted on
docs/audit/PG0_FORENSIC_AUDIT.md because SALE-02 had edited the same table
row in the meantime. That is my fault twice over: touching a shared roadmap
document in every feature patch turns one file into a permanent merge
magnet, for no benefit the git history does not already provide. The doc
edit is gone from this patch and will not come back in feature work.

THE DEFECT

The largest surface on this site is its geography: 100 city pages and 11
corridor pages out of 261 indexed URLs. Not one of them contained a form.

Their primary button, twice per city page, was:

    <a href="/#quote" className="btn btn-copper btn-lg">

That is a CROSS-PAGE anchor. A homeowner who searched "hardwood flooring
etobicoke", landed on the Etobicoke page, and pressed the main call to
action was sent to the homepage to scroll for a form. The only contact
mechanism on the page itself was a bare tel: link in the sixth section. The
corridor pages had no call to action at all.

A REGRESSION WITH A COMMIT MESSAGE ALREADY WRITTEN ABOUT IT

EstimateForm's own docblock records F-160: "Every commercial page's primary
button pointed at /#quote. That anchor is on a DIFFERENT url... <form> count
0, <input> count 0." That fix reached /services, /pricing, /commercial,
/realtors and the four Toronto landing pages. It never reached the 111 pages
that carry the entire geographic footprint — six service pages got a form,
111 local-intent pages did not. geo-conversion.test.ts now holds it.

WHAT MEAS-01 AND MEAS-02 BOUGHT

`source` carries the city or the corridor, so a lead from Etobicoke is
distinguishable from one from Oakville in the funnel ledger. "Which cities
actually produce deposits" stops being an assumption — and the answer is
what should decide where the next real job photograph comes from, because
content/job-cards.ts holds five real jobs, all in Toronto proper, so 96 of
these pages carry true prose about the place and no evidence this business
has worked there. That gap is not closed by writing. It is closed by
photographing real work, and the ledger says which city first.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO

It does not prefill a location. `source` says which PAGE produced the lead;
it is never a claim about where the visitor is, and it does not reach the
address field. Somebody reading the Whitby page from a Toronto office is not
a Whitby job, and the postal code they type is the only location this
business acts on. A test asserts no location prop reaches the form.

It does not move the form above the local content. A page whose entire job
is to establish that this business works in this place spends that
credibility if it leads with the ask. Order: why you should believe we work
here, then the ask, then the NAP block — which stays last and stays
interpolated from BUSINESS_NAP, because a local page stating the address
differently from the homepage is the commonest reason a local entity fails
to resolve.

KNOWN AND DELIBERATELY NOT HERE

Fourteen other templates still link to /#quote without a form: the footer,
404, the portal pages, /team, /about, /technical-library, /framework,
/resources, /service-areas, /where-we-work, /guides/[slug], /products/
floorforge. Most are navigational and the homepage anchor is the right
target. /service-areas, /where-we-work and /guides/[slug] are arguable, and
that is a separate decision rather than something to fold quietly into a
patch about the detail pages.

PARSE-SCAN CAUGHT ME

The first version of the test asserted on 'source={`service-area-${city.
slug}`}' — a `${` inside a plain string, which parse-scan flags because that
shape is almost always a template literal typed with the wrong quotes. It
was intentional here and the rule is still right, so the needle is split
rather than excepted. I had not re-run parse-scan after adding the test;
ship.sh would have caught it at step 6, and did not only because the patch
failed at step 2.

Verified: 64 of 66 guards. verify:css needs postcss from node_modules,
absent in this sandbox. verify:hygiene fails on the tracked
ECOWOODS_SALE_03_geo_conversion.patch sitting on origin/main from the web
upload — HYG-02 doing its job on a real artifact, cleared the moment ship.sh
applies this. parse-scan 614 files, zero diagnostics. Resolving typecheck
clean on both templates. 21 assertions.

